  "notes": "Schedule 1-A Part V line 36b, v2 successor to v1: line 35 when the return is married filing jointly, the spouse was born before January 2, 1961 (and did not die in 2025 before reaching 65), and the spouse has a valid SSN; otherwise 0. spouse_over_65 is a required input with no default, so it is read, and asked, only on a joint return: the joint-return test now comes first. Every other return publishes 0 without reading it. The valid-SSN conditional_dependency_set and the rest of v1's expression are unchanged."
